{
  "note": "Self-written registration confirmations and ticket orders for made-up events, venues and attendees: a confirmation of registration for a conference, and a confirmation of a concert ticket order, in each language. The events set holds flyers and programmes; this set holds what the attendee gets back after signing up or buying. Each is in a clean version and a planted one that differs only on the lines below. They run as business/email, since each is the confirmation email an attendee receives. Each mistake names its kind, the line it is on, the text the clean line has there (clean) and the planted line has instead (planted), and the rule expected to report it on that line. The conference's deadline is a deadline for changing the registration, the concert's a payment deadline; both are named for deadline-after-event. The doors-open time later than the start time is named for time-order: the conference gives it as a row of its programme table, the concert as a labelled list item (Doors open: 17:30). The number of tickets or attendees given two ways (a table row and a sentence) is named for fact-conflict. The line-total plants change the unit price, not the amount, so the total the grand-total plant is compared with does not move, and the count plants change the sentence, not the table row the line-total plant multiplies. Each plant was also run alone on its clean document, so no plant depends on another. yarn planted tickets scores them; expected.json is the committed score.",
